{
  "biological_interpretation": "The evidence supports a thalamic KMT2D/KDM6A MLL3/4-adjacent module that is not simply shared by all KMT2/KDM6 paralogs or by CBP loss.",
  "caveats": [
    "Neither Kmt2d nor Kdm6a showed FDR-confirmed target-transcript depletion.",
    "The Kdm6a arm had only one FDR gene and the Kmt2d relation was based on a restricted top-500 Kdm6a vector."
  ],
  "cell_types": [
    "151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut"
  ],
  "exact_observed_result": "Kmt2d produced 314 FDR genes in 151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut, and the weak Kdm6a signature aligned with Kmt2d on Ntng1, Nell1, Ptpn5, Cyp46a1, Tspan33, Thy1 and Mical2; Crebbp placed Kmt2d/Kdm6a only in its weak positive neighbor tail.",
